course: dictionary
lesson: 1579
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. The word chart is a good example. «Jayden made a turn chart in four colours and stuck it on Mia's wall.» Here a chart is a drawing that shows information.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another sentence. «In 1642 the Dutch sailor Abel Tasman reached Tasmania and New Zealand, and in the 1760s and 1770s the British captain James Cook made three great voyages and mapped coasts so well that some of his charts were used for centuries.» Here a chart is a map of the sea used by sailors.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. «A chart, jar or app that shows your progress helps you keep going.» A chart is a drawing that shows information. Does "a map that shows your progress" make sense? No. So the meaning is different here, and you must read more carefully.
fact: Chart can be a noun (a chart, charts) or a verb (chart, charts, charted, charting).
fact: As a noun, a chart is a drawing that shows information, such as a graph, table or diagram, like a bar chart.
fact: A chart can also be a map of the sea or sky used by sailors or pilots.
fact: The charts means lists of the most popular songs, as in «top the charts».
fact: As a verb, to chart means to make a map of something, or to follow and record how something changes, as in «chart your progress».
exercise: «Jayden made a turn chart in four colours and stuck it on Mia's wall.» In this sentence, what is a chart? | A list of the most popular songs | A pilot's map of the sky | A map of the sea used by sailors | *A drawing that shows information
exercise: «In 1642 the Dutch sailor Abel Tasman reached Tasmania and New Zealand, and ... James Cook mapped coasts so well that some of his charts were used for centuries.» What does chart mean here? | The charts, the top songs | To follow how something changes | *A map of the sea used by sailors | A bar chart in maths class
exercise: «A chart, jar or app that shows your progress helps you keep going.» Which meaning of chart fits the phrase «chart your progress»? | The list of most popular songs | *To follow and record how something changes | A map of the sky used by pilots | A drawing of a bar chart
test: «An optometrist tests vision with a letter chart whose lines get smaller.» What does chart mean in «letter chart»? | A list of the most popular songs | *A sheet that shows information, here letters to read | A map of the sea | To draw a map of a coast
test: Ella says «top the charts» means to climb to the top of a mountain. What does the charts mean here? | A map of the sea used by sailors | Tables of the tallest mountains | A drawing of a pie chart in maths | *Lists of the most popular songs
exam: Ella will chart how fast her plant grows each week. What does chart mean here? | A drawing that shows information | *To record how something changes | A list of the most popular songs | A map of the sea
